.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-piv-keys-generate-batch 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-piv\-keys\-generate\-batch \- Generate the same algorithm into several slots in one batch (one management authentication, progress per slot)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-piv\-keys\-generate\-batch\fR <\fB\-\-slots\fR> [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-algorithm\fR] [\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-pin\-policy\fR] [\fB\-\-touch\-policy\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-management\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate the same algorithm into several slots in one batch (one management authentication, progress per slot)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-slots\fR \fI<SLOTS>\fR
Comma\-separated PIV slots (e.g. 9a,9c,9d,9e)
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-algorithm\fR \fI<ALGORITHM>\fR [default: rsa2048]
Algorithm to use in key generation
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
rsa1024
.IP \(bu 2
rsa2048
.IP \(bu 2
rsa3072
.IP \(bu 2
rsa4096
.IP \(bu 2
ecc\-p256
.IP \(bu 2
ecc\-p384
.IP \(bu 2
ecc\-p521
.IP \(bu 2
secp256k1
.IP \(bu 2
sm2
.IP \(bu 2
ed25519
.IP \(bu 2
x25519
.IP \(bu 2
ml\-dsa65
.IP \(bu 2
ml\-kem768
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fI<OUTPUT_DIR>\fR [default: .]
Directory for the public keys (`<slot>.pem` / `<slot>.der`)
.TP
\fB\-\-pin\-policy\fR \fI<PIN_POLICY>\fR
PIN policy for the keys
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
never
.IP \(bu 2
once
.IP \(bu 2
always
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-touch\-policy\fR \fI<TOUCH_POLICY>\fR
Touch policy for the keys
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
never
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
cached
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: pem]
Output format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
pem
.IP \(bu 2
der
.RE
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-management\-key\fR \fI<MANAGEMENT_KEY>\fR
Current management key as 48 hex characters (prompted when needed)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
